A||||9||mrfixit58||The Fiero... The Most Versatile Spors Car... Ever?||||3||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||04-09-2001||11:15 AM||||I was talking to someone the other day and, of course, the topic of Fieros came up. He asked me, "Why are you so into those little cars?". Well, That started a whole dissertation on the merits of our beloved little sports car. I mentioned to him that the Fiero is the ONLY mid-engine mass produced production car ever mad in the US. <P>But one thing that kept coming up was how versatile the little sports car is. Except, maybe, for the VW Bug, I can't think of any model of car that has had more external body modifications designed for it than the Fiero. As far a the motor, I can't think of ANY model that can come close to number of different motors that I've seen in the Fiero. The car is destined to go down in history as the best all around platform for the custom car industry. Every time I pick up a kit car magazine of some publication that discusses this industry, the Fiero name pops up.<P>No real purpose here except to rant about the attributes of the Fiero. It just continues to amaze me.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000001||Wolfhound||04-09-2001||01:14 PM||||Roy, Excellent point, and well said. Another factor to consider is the bad rap, that the Fiero recieved from the press, has made it possible for those of us who have to watch their money pretty close to get them for a reasonable price.<P>Also, the fact that all body panels from five years of production are interchangable, as well as most other parts, with the limited differences in the 87 and 88,s.<P>Within this year (Popular Mechanics, PS or MI, I forget which)had an artical about a future car that could change skins to fit your specific preferences. My first thought was "they are going to invent a Fiero?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Coy<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||04-09-2001||03:51 PM||||Coy,<P>I would be interested in that article. If you can find out which magazine and when it was published, I'd like to know.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||danny boy||04-09-2001||05:39 PM|||| Me and a friend were discussing this very same topic last night while messin with his 3400 swap. I did something a few days earlier and the question "So why are you still messing around with Fieros?" came up. Thats why. anything I can possibly want to do to a car I can do with my Fiero. Any engine I can afford,any brakes,suspension, body changes I can do with my cars. Gotta love em.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
